[[2047,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The circuit is controlled by the hazard warning lights switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The intermittent device is located on the steering column switch unit H5. It is connected to earth at pin 7 of connector A and receives a supply signal at pin 7 of connector D through switch H20:</p><ul><li>when the hazard lights are not off, the supply is controlled\nby the ignition (INT/A) through the line for fuse <strong>B10</strong> up\nto 2/99 or from fuse <strong>F6</strong> of the additional fuse box <strong>B98B</strong> from\n2/99</li><li>when the hazard lights are on, the supply is direct from\nthe battery through fuse <strong>F9</strong> of the junction unit <strong>B1</strong> and\nmaxifuse <strong>J/B1</strong> of <strong>B5</strong> up to 2/99 or of <strong>B99</strong> from\n2/99.</li></ul><p>The intermittent device produces a signal\nwhich supplies the switch for the direction indicators on the steering\ncolumn switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and the switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The operation, in one direction or another,\nof the steering column switch lever \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               supplies the right\ndirection indicators (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F21</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F31</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) or the\nleft ones (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>At the same time the warning light, located\nin the rev counter module  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , comes on.</p><p>Pressing the switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               closes three\ncontacts which simultaneously supply all the lights (right branch\nand left branch) close and the red LED in the actual switch which\nlights up the symbol in flashing mode.</p><p>In switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               there is also a green\nLED which comes on when the ignition is switched on (INT/A).</p><p>All the hazard warning lights are also operated\nby the alarm system control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (pins 1 and 2 of connector\nB), which is connected directly to the light power supply (\n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3234737\">E7015</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p>"]]